From 13699cf402b252286c674e9e82af30359524fe09 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Charliechen114514 <725610365@qq.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 23:22:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] rockchip: boot_mode: handle BOOT_LOADER with rockusb

setup_boot_mode() handles BOOT_FASTBOOT and BOOT_UMS but drops
BOOT_LOADER on the floor, losing the vendor 'reboot loader' experience.
Wire it the same way as its neighbours: preboot drops into rockusb on
eMMC. The kernel side writes the magic via the topeet reboot-mode DT
node (pmu0_grf + 0x80 = 0xfd588080 = this register).

Signed-off-by: Charliechen114514 <725610365@qq.com>
---
 arch/arm/mach-rockchip/boot_mode.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/boot_mode.c b/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/boot_mode.c
index 55e9456668a..08dd1f20b64 100644
--- a/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/boot_mode.c
+++ b/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/boot_mode.c
@@ -105,6 +105,10 @@ int setup_boot_mode(void)
 		debug("%s: enter UMS!\n", __func__);
 		env_set("preboot", "setenv preboot; ums mmc 0");
 		break;
+	case BOOT_LOADER:
+		debug("%s: enter rockusb!\n", __func__);
+		env_set("preboot", "setenv preboot; rockusb 0 mmc 0");
+		break;
 	}
 
 	return 0;
